Consider the following agent actions and subsequent observations; note that the set of actions were taken together and in-order, and all observations were made after the full set of actions. Your task is to determine whether the set of observations are caused by the set of actions. That is, were the observations a response (whether by a human, another agent, the environment, etc.) to the actions taken? If the observations are a direct response (e.g. feedback, tool use response, etc.) to the actions, respond with 'YES'. If the observations are unrelated to the actions, respond with 'NO'. You are also provided with some context (the observations that occurred previous to the actions block, so Context (Observations) --> Actions --> Observations), but these should not be evaluated when determining causality; only evaluate the blocks labeled Actions and Observations.

Context:
{context}

Actions:
{actions}

Observations:
{observations}

Your response should be a single word: either 'YES' or 'NO'.
